00:20:49.200 --> 00:20:52.710
In order to debug a microservice
using the Cloud Code extension,

00:20:52.710 --> 00:20:54.335
we need to do two things.

00:20:54.335 --> 00:20:56.710
The first thing is to ensure
that the Docker file that we

00:20:56.710 --> 00:20:58.930
are using is debug-ready.

00:20:58.930 --> 00:21:05.800
So in the case of node.js, that
means using the inspect flag

00:21:05.800 --> 00:21:07.100
in the start-up command.

00:21:07.100 --> 00:21:09.850
And we have similar instructions
available for other languages

00:21:09.850 --> 00:21:11.583
in our documentation.

00:21:11.583 --> 00:21:13.000
And the second
thing we need to do

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:16.035
is to add the corresponding
debug configuration.

00:21:16.035 --> 00:21:17.660
Currently, there are
no configurations.

00:21:17.660 --> 00:21:21.130
We can add a configuration using
an Add Configuration option

00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:21.675
there.

00:21:21.675 --> 00:21:24.980
And we can select the
Cloud Code debug here.

00:21:24.980 --> 00:21:28.020
But I will add debug confusion
a slightly different way.

00:21:28.020 --> 00:21:33.210
I'll go to the .vscode folder
and add a new file called

00:21:33.210 --> 00:21:34.920
launch.json.

00:21:34.920 --> 00:21:37.300
And I'll go to the
Configurations section

00:21:37.300 --> 00:21:39.250
here and press Control-Space.

00:21:39.250 --> 00:21:41.650
Here, we can see a list
of Cloud Code debug

00:21:41.650 --> 00:21:43.535
snippets available for us.

00:21:43.535 --> 00:21:45.910
And because the voting services
is written using node.js,

00:21:45.910 --> 00:21:49.100
we'll go ahead and use
the node.js snippet.

00:21:49.100 --> 00:21:51.460
Here, you'll see a number of
options, but in most cases,

00:21:51.460 --> 00:21:54.640
you'll have to worry
about just three of these.

00:21:54.640 --> 00:21:55.900
So the first is a name.

00:21:55.900 --> 00:21:59.830
Let's name it debug voting.

00:21:59.830 --> 00:22:01.330
And the second one
is a local route.

00:22:01.330 --> 00:22:03.330
This is for the debugger
to know the source code

00:22:03.330 --> 00:22:04.770
location of your microservice.

00:22:04.770 --> 00:22:06.732
The source code of
the voting services

00:22:06.732 --> 00:22:07.940
is in the source folder here.

00:22:07.940 --> 00:22:09.670
So we'll go ahead
and update that.

00:22:14.790 --> 00:22:17.030
And the third thing
is the pod selector.

00:22:17.030 --> 00:22:20.370
This is to uniquely identify
the microservice pod

00:22:20.370 --> 00:22:21.900
in the cluster.

00:22:21.900 --> 00:22:23.400
So we'll go to that
voting.yaml file

00:22:23.400 --> 00:22:25.800
and see the ports
that we are using.

00:22:25.800 --> 00:22:27.750
Looks like we are
using app:voting.

00:22:27.750 --> 00:22:30.380
So let's copy this and use
it in the launch.json file.

00:22:34.450 --> 00:22:36.470
And because we have
updated the Docker file,

00:22:36.470 --> 00:22:38.105
let's do one more deployment.

00:22:43.057 --> 00:22:45.390
And now, the application has
been deployed successfully.

00:22:45.390 --> 00:22:47.060
And now, we have
everything we need

00:22:47.060 --> 00:22:49.540
to debug this microservice.

00:22:49.540 --> 00:22:53.370
So I'll go to the
index.js file, and we'll

00:22:53.370 --> 00:22:55.170
set a big point in
the first method

00:22:55.170 --> 00:22:57.990
here, and then go
to the Debug window

00:22:57.990 --> 00:23:00.462
and press Debug Voting button.

00:23:03.380 --> 00:23:05.390
Next, let's try to
submit the vote,

00:23:05.390 --> 00:23:08.180
and the breakpoint has been hit.

00:23:08.180 --> 00:23:10.430
Now, we are [INAUDIBLE]
the application deployed

00:23:10.430 --> 00:23:12.110
in a Kubernetes cluster.

00:23:12.110 --> 00:23:14.330
So we can see all the
properties of the request

00:23:14.330 --> 00:23:16.700
object and the response object.

00:23:16.700 --> 00:23:20.110
And we can step through
the code line by line.

00:23:20.110 --> 00:23:22.040
And we also have
some debug windows

00:23:22.040 --> 00:23:24.000
