00:23:45.900 --> 00:23:47.470
Let's step through.

00:23:47.470 --> 00:23:49.310
Looks like we are
trying to access

00:23:49.310 --> 00:23:52.200
a property on the vote subject
here, which is currently

00:23:52.200 --> 00:23:54.500
undefined.

00:23:54.500 --> 00:23:56.550
And it's failing with an
internal server error.

00:23:56.550 --> 00:23:59.680
So let's stop debugging,
fix this issue.

00:23:59.680 --> 00:24:03.033
We'll instantiate with an empty
object when it's undefined,

00:24:03.033 --> 00:24:03.700
and deploy this.

00:24:10.980 --> 00:24:14.040
Let's see if it's
working this time.

00:24:14.040 --> 00:24:16.530
And now, we're able to
post the vote successfully.

00:24:16.530 --> 00:24:17.040
Awesome.

00:24:17.040 --> 00:24:18.582
So let's take a
quick summary of what

00:24:18.582 --> 00:24:19.960
we have done in this section.

00:24:19.960 --> 00:24:21.720
So we started with
an empty directory

00:24:21.720 --> 00:24:24.360
and added the source code
for the microservices

00:24:24.360 --> 00:24:25.740
along with the Docker files.

00:24:25.740 --> 00:24:28.110
And then we added the
Kubernetes manifest that are

00:24:28.110 --> 00:24:30.980
needed for this application.

00:24:30.980 --> 00:24:33.140
And then we created our
first deployment profile

00:24:33.140 --> 00:24:36.860
for our local
environment, and then we

00:24:36.860 --> 00:24:38.960
diagnosed the deployment
issues with the help

00:24:38.960 --> 00:24:43.240
of the logs that were streamed
directly to the output window.

00:24:43.240 --> 00:24:44.770
And finally, we
were able to debug

00:24:44.770 --> 00:24:47.440
an application deployed
in the Kubernetes cluster

00:24:47.440 --> 00:24:48.790
and fix the bug.

00:24:48.790 --> 00:24:51.340
Awesome.

00:24:51.340 --> 00:24:54.010
So far, we are only able to see
this application on my machine

00:24:54.010 --> 00:24:55.060
