00:38:23.460 --> 00:38:26.940
another command called Cloud
Code continuous deploy.

00:38:26.940 --> 00:38:29.342
Previously, we have seen the
Cloud Code deploy command

00:38:29.342 --> 00:38:31.050
that does all the
grunt work of deploying

00:38:31.050 --> 00:38:32.700
an application to a cluster.

00:38:32.700 --> 00:38:34.640
And the Cloud Code
continuous deploy command

00:38:34.640 --> 00:38:37.300
take it one step further.

00:38:37.300 --> 00:38:39.330
What this command does
is it continuously

00:38:39.330 --> 00:38:42.200
watches the application
directory for any changes.

00:38:42.200 --> 00:38:44.580
And when it detects any
changes, it automatically

00:38:44.580 --> 00:38:47.890
deploys the application
to the cluster.

00:38:47.890 --> 00:38:50.400
This command will come
in particularly handy

00:38:50.400 --> 00:38:53.697
when you want to rapidly
iterate on all code.

00:38:53.697 --> 00:38:54.780
So let's see it in action.

00:38:59.090 --> 00:39:02.910
So I"ll go the command pallet
